@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Accessibility statement"; }
<h1>Accessibility statement</h1>
<p>ToolShare is meant to be usable by everyone, including people who use screen readers, keyboards only, voice control, magnification or high contrast settings.</p>
<h2>What we do</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Every page works with a keyboard. A "Skip to main content" link is the first item on each page.</li>
  <li>Pages use headings, landmarks, labelled forms, and tables with headers so screen readers can navigate them.</li>
  <li>Status is shown with words, not colour alone. Messages are announced to screen readers.</li>
  <li>Text colours meet WCAG 2.2 AA contrast in light and dark mode, and the page follows your device's contrast and reduced-motion settings.</li>
  <li>The layout adapts from small phones to wide screens, and works when text is enlarged up to 200 percent. Buttons and links are at least 44 pixels tall.</li>
  <li>Forms use plain language, visible labels, and error messages that explain how to fix the problem.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Known limits</h2>
<p>This site has been checked with automated tools and by keyboard. It has not yet had a full audit with assistive technology users. If something does not work for you, please open an issue in the project repository.</p>
